  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Centre pushes States to speed up PNG adoption, seeks district-level officers to drive LPG-to-gas transition",
      "link": "https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/centre-pushes-states-to-speed-up-png-adoption-seeks-district-level-officers-to-drive-lpg-to-gas-transition/article71380405.ece",
      "description": "The push for faster adoption of gas piped to households for cooking purposes, called PNG, follows the disruption to India's LPG supply chains during the West Asia crisis earlier this year.",
      "source_name": "The Hindu National",
      "published": "2026-08-23T08:41:24"
    },
    {
      "title": "Central govt asks states to appoint nodal officers to speed up PNG adoption",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/economy/news/central-govt-asks-states-to-appoint-nodal-officers-to-speed-up-png-adoption-126082300237_1.html",
      "description": "The Petroleum Ministry has asked states and Union Territories to provide district-level administrative support to accelerate the shift of households from LPG to piped natural gas (PNG), seeking appointment of nodal officers to coordinate with gas distributors and oil marketing companies.\nIn an August 21 letter to state chief secretaries, Petroleum Secretary Neeraj Mittal said PNG, as a safer, cleaner and more efficient cooking fuel, has an important role in advancing India's energy transition while reducing the logistics burden associated with LPG distribution and improving consumer convenience.\n\"PNG brings a safer, cleaner and more efficient cooking fuel, playing a critical role in advancing the country's energy transition objectives. Its accelerated adoption contributes to reducing the logistics burden associated with LPG distribution, enhancing consumer convenience, and improving utilisation of CGD infrastructure created through substantial public and private investment,\" Mittal .",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-08-23T07:26:28"
    }
  ]
